An upcoming live-action ''[[Star Wars]]'' '''film''' set during the [[New Republic Era]] by [[Dave Filoni]] is currently in development.<ref name="New movies" /> The film will feature a conflict between the [[New Republic]] and [[Imperial Remnants]]<ref name="Variety Celebration">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/star-wars-movies-dave-filoni-james-mangold-1235576542|text='Star Wars' Movies: James Mangold, Dave Filoni to Direct New Films|author=Manori Ravindran|date=2023-04-07|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20231121200640}}</ref> and will close out the stories told in ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'', [[Star Wars: Ahsoka|''Ahsoka'']], ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'' and other related series on [[Disney+]].<ref name="New movies" />

==Development==
During a presentation at [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]] Investor Day [[2020]], [[Lucasfilm]] President [[Kathleen Kennedy]] announced that interconnected stories between series such as ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' and [[Star Wars: Ahsoka|''Ahsoka'']] would cross over and culminate in a "climactic story event."<ref name="Investor2020">{{DisneyCompany|url=disney-investor-day-2020|text=Disney Investor Day 2020}}</ref>

On [[April 7]], [[2023]], at a panel at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]], the project was revealed to be a theatrical film helmed by director [[Dave Filoni]]. A news post on [[StarWars.com]] the same day confirmed that the film would "close out" the stories started in series like ''The Mandalorian''.<ref name="New movies" /> In an interview with [[Wikipedia:IGN|''IGN'']] at the convention, Kennedy discussed how the genesis for the film had started over a decade prior and evolved organically into the current iteration of the project. She also revealed that Filoni would write the film.<ref name="KK IGN Interview" /> Also at Celebration, Filoni was interviewed by [[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']] and revealed that the film would center around a conflict between the [[New Republic]] and [[Imperial Remnants]].<ref name="Variety Celebration" /> When interviewed by [[Wikipedia:Empire (magazine)|''Empire'']] on [[May 5]], Filoni discussed how he wants the film to deal with moments that "define an era," in this case the space between [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']] and [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']].<ref name="Empire Interview">{{WebCite|url=https://www.empireonline.com/movies/news/dave-filoni-star-wars-movie-will-be-moments-define-era-exclusive|text=Dave Filoni Teases What His Star Wars Movie Will Be: 'You're Looking For Moments That Define An Era' &ndash; Exclusive|author=Ben Travis|date=2023-05-05|work=[[Wikipedia:Empire (magazine)|''Empire'']]|archivedate=20231010213649}}</ref>

